Z||000014||btoth||11-26-2001||12:45 PM||||    <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>Another forum that I frequent is:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.labusas.org" TARGET=_blank>www.labusas.org</A> <P>It's pretty cool. Entertraining read.<P>Sly</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What do they talk about there?<P><BR>I visit the forums at <A HREF="http://www.gamedev.net" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gamedev.net.</A>   I've been looking for any other cool programming related forums that get lots of traffic and quick responses. (Like this forum!)     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 11-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||Fformula88||11-26-2001||02:47 PM||||I also spend some time on  <A HREF="http://www.probetalk.com" TARGET=_blank>www.probetalk.com</A> .  Not as much as here, and in fact I use my same screen name there as I do here!  <P>My daily driver is a 97 Probe SE.<P>There are some knowledgable guys over there, but they tend to be a lot more ricey!  They also do not care to much for the Fiero, and I hhave had to call some of the guys here in for some reinforcement to help educate them!  They at least tend to stay away from big flame wars!<P>For anyone who wants to see more forums at PFF, probetalk is a good example why NOT to expand.  They have broken the board down into so many small little forums I feel it has lost a sense of community.  They have also created locked forums where only certain members who are part of their "clique" can get into, which has further divided it up.  <P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
